  "diagnosis_text": "### Diagnosis\n\nThe physical topology and ports are up, but the forwarding rules for the **s1\u2013s5 path are incorrect in both directions**.\n\nEvidence:\n\n- Topology shows the direct link:\n  - `s1 port 2 \u2194 s5 port 1`\n- Both ports are enabled.\n- `h1 \u2192 h5` ping: **100% loss**\n- Adjacent connectivity works:\n  - `h1 \u2192 h2`: 0% loss\n  - `h2 \u2192 h3`: 0% loss\n  - `h3 \u2192 h4`: 0% loss\n  - `h4 \u2192 h5`: 0% loss\n\nFaulty flow entries:\n\n- On **s1**, traffic destined for h5 (`00:00:00:00:00:05`) is sent to **port 1**, which leads to s2. It should be sent to **port 2**, which leads directly to s5.\n- On **s5**, traffic destined for h1 (`00:00:00:00:00:01`) is sent to **port 2**, which leads to s4. It should be sent to **port 1**, which leads directly to s1.\n\n### Localisation\n\nThe fault is localized to the **h1/h5 forwarding rules on s1 and s5**, not to the host interfaces or physical inter-switch links.\n\nThe required next step is to regenerate or correct those two forwarding entries:\n\n- `s1: destination h5 \u2192 output port 2`\n- `s5: destination h1 \u2192 output port 1`\n\nThere are also stale/inactive duplicate ONOS device records, but the five active switches and five physical links are present and operational; those records do not appear to be the immediate cause.",
